	(text_box "Source: OpenFC-Lite hardware/pads.kicad_sch (CAM frame: pads + SH1.0 SM03B plug), adapted to the JST SUR 0.8 mm SM03B-SURS-TF(LF)(SN) (D63/D64, IO-SET row 3: BetaFPV C03 and the Matrix-recommended cameras).\n\nPlug and pads in parallel: J32 pin 1 VIDEO_IN, 2 GND, 3 +5V_CAM, tabs 4/5 GND; pads CAM / GND / 5V (J23 J25 J24). On the board the plug faces inward and the pads sit in front of its mouth: plug OR solder in one mating zone (D72).\n\nVIDEO_IN -> OSD front end (TLV7031 sync + SN74LVC1G3157, OSD sheet), netclass Analog (OSD directive). +5V_CAM = +5V after FB1 120 R + C15 10 uF (POWER), 0.12 A. Video return: CAM GND pad and plug pin 2 enter L2 at the CAM pad (spec 11).\n\nGate G1 still open: pin order provisional until calipers + photo on a C03 lead and the MX2 CAM IN. With GND in the middle a mirrored footprint puts 5 V on the camera's video output. G1 = 1.0 mm pitch -> SM03B-SRSS-TB(LF)(SN), same pins."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.5 172.72 0)
		(size 109.22 60.96)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "16c1832b-1fcc-545a-ba1e-b0edbad236d3")
	)
	(text_box "H1-H3: the 25.5 mm M1.4 pattern (D73) is cut in Edge.Cuts (ear holes with flange keep-outs, spec 7), so the symbols are excluded from the board (FLOORPLAN 'For P4'), BOM and CPL; footprint kept as reference. No net (non-plated; GND annulus = O16). LOGO1 (incutec, B.Silkscreen) is a board-only footprint, no symbol."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 261.62 0)
		(size 76.2 21.59)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6901b8ab-f643-5e9f-b8f1-b9fd2b87c3cb")
	)
	(text_box "Source: OpenFC-Lite hardware/pads.kicad_sch (JST SH SM04B plug in a frame; there it carries a UART). The USB pinout, D7 and the VBUS flag are new (D57). Commons block USB_C_GCT4105_USBLC6 checked, not used (USB-C and a 6-pin ESD part).\n\nJ31 JST BM04B-SRSS-TB(LF)(SN) as in bom_plan (vertical, bottom): 1 GND, 2 D- (USB_D_N), 3 D+ (USB_D_P), 4 VBUS, tabs 5/6 GND = BetaFPV 'USB(GND DM DP 5V)' order (bom_plan, IO-SET row 6, LIBRARY D57). Pin 1 = GND is inferred: continuity check with a BetaFPV Type-C to SH1.0 adapter on prototype 1. D72 moves J31 to the side-entry SM04B-SRSS-TB(LF)(SN) (lib:SM04B-SRSS-TB, same pins 1-6) once bom_plan carries it: a field swap.\n\nD7 TPD2EUSB30DRTR (TI SLVSAC2G): pin 1 D+, 2 D-, 3 GND (Table 5-1); VRWM 5.5 V, IO abs max 6 V, so a D+/D- short to VBUS survives; 8 V clamp at 1 A, 0.7 pF, IEC 61000-4-2 8 kV contact, -40..85 C. It sits at J31, ahead of the 27 R R42/R43 at the RP2354A (RP2350A sheet). Layout per DS 10.1: next to J31, protected traces straight with rounded corners, no unprotected trace beside the J31-D7 stretch, GND pin by via-in-pad into L2. USB pair 90 ohm, length-matched (D33); netclass USB from the directive on USB_D_P (_P/_N pair).\n\nVBUS is a hierarchical net (LINEUP A11) to POWER: U24 SGM40661 OVP IN + C131 100 nF take the hot-plug and over-voltage duty (D57). PWR_FLAG here: J31 is the only source of VBUS. A cable with pins 1/4 swapped puts -5 V on VBUS (unprotected, as on the Matrix)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 254 73.66 0)
		(size 149.86 43.18)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "69a05841-5488-576d-9dc8-e8ff87250b46")
	)
	(text_box "Source: OpenFC-Lite-Mini hardware/pads.kicad_sch (digital video pads), new pad set (D13/D16).\n\nVHD = +5V_HD from U5 TPS22810 (on with HD_EN AND cell > 2.8-3.1 V, POWER), 1.20 A budget; O4 Lite input 3.7-13.2 V. TX1 = UART1_TX (GPIO4) -> O4 RX, RX1 = UART1_RX (GPIO5) <- O4 TX: MSP DisplayPort; no SBUS pad (D16). Cut DJI cable: red -> VHD, black + brown -> GND, white -> TX1, grey -> RX1, yellow open (RP0 only with the EXT-USER-PADS preset).\n\nAnalog builds: TX1/RX1 are a free hardware UART, or I2C0 via the I2C-HD preset (IO-SET row 8).\n\nP4-11: the O4 stays unpowered until HD_EN, so its TX cannot drive RX1 before IOVDD (FT pads limited to 3.63 V unpowered, PINMAP F16).\n\nCopper only (DNP, out of BOM and CPL, LINEUP A16)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 309.88 172.72 0)
		(size 93.98 60.96)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6faaff37-4c41-503d-a2e5-8c533365b63a")
	)
	(text_box "Source: OpenFC-Lite-Mini hardware/pads.kicad_sch ('Free UART (GPS)' group).\n\nTP0 = PIOUART0_TX (GPIO2), RP0 = PIOUART0_RX (GPIO3), PIO1 shared with the LED strip (PINMAP F5), half duplex and inversion capable. 8N1 only: Betaflight's RP2350 PIO UART rejects even parity, so SBUS / 8E2 receivers use the EXT-USER-PADS preset (hardware UART0 on these pads; 8E2 needs a Betaflight release with the uart_hw.c fix); I2C1 via I2C-USER (IO-SET 2.3).\n\n5V = +5V (TPS2116 output, 0.05 A allowance, spec 5.1) and GND for the device.\n\nP4-11 (pads, power-up): GPIO2/3 are FT pads, 5.5 V tolerant with IOVDD up but limited to 3.63 V while IOVDD is still 0 (PINMAP F16). The 5V pad comes up before +3V3 (LDO start after the mux): use 3.3 V-logic devices (GPS, receivers); a 5 V-logic TX on RP0 can exceed that limit during the ramp.\n\nSilk TP0 RP0 5V GND; copper only (DNP, out of BOM and CPL, LINEUP A16)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 172.72 0)
		(size 76.2 60.96)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "77916f28-e410-5829-94d0-64091162b188")
	)
	(text_box "Source: OpenFC-Lite-Mini hardware/pads.kicad_sch (LED-strip and buzzer pads).\n\nRow GND LED 5V BZ- (D63/D64): the strip gets its own GND pad J33 (supersedes D27).\n\nLED = LED_STRIP driven straight from GPIO8 (PIO1 ws2812; D52 BR-04: no translator, no series resistor, Matrix II parity). A WS2812B on 5 V asks VIH 0.7 VDD = 3.5 V; the 3.3 V drive works on the common whoop strips, a level problem shows as a dead first LED (bench check, V9).\n\n5V = +5V for the strip (0.20 A allowance, analog mode, spec 5.1) and the buzzer +. BZ- = BUZZER-: drain of the AP1606 low-side switch Q26, gate on GPIO17 (BEEPER_INVERTED, RP2350A sheet); the buzzer sits between 5V and BZ-.\n\nCopper only (DNP, out of BOM and CPL, LINEUP A16)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 104.14 172.72 0)
		(size 76.2 60.96)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a579dd9f-e3a6-5b42-9352-66d81a91eea9")
	)
	(text_box "Source: OpenFC-Lite-Mini hardware/pads.kicad_sch (Conn_01x01 pad, pin down, rail symbol at the wire end).\n\nJ2 '+' = +BATT_IN, J3 '-' = GND: BT2.0 pigtail (22 AWG, user-fitted) through plated D1.1 holes in 3.0 x 2.0 mm pads (lib:BattPad_3.0x2.0mm_PTH1.1), >= 12 power vias each into the pours (spec 4.10, D72 power plan: +BATT_IN into L4 + L1/L6, GND into L2/L5). Silk '+' / '-' 2.0 mm and '1S' (spec 13).\n\n1S LiPo/LiHV only, 3.0-4.35 V (D14). D1 SMF5.0A TVS, the pad bulk and the shunt R1 sit on POWER, which also holds the +BATT_IN and GND PWR_FLAGs. Netclass VBAT: directive here on +BATT_IN at J2.\n\nCopper only: DNP, out of BOM and CPL (LINEUP A16)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 54.61 0)
		(size 48.26 62.23)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d9604d41-3957-5eb9-a496-8e9027dc020d")
	)
	(text_box "Source: new (D65: plug-ready lands as on the BetaFPV Matrix 1S 5IN1 II), drawn in the house pad style. One land per motor, lib:MotorPad_PicoBlade_1x03_P1.25mm_PTH0.5: pads 1 / 2 / 3 = Mn_C / Mn_B / Mn_A = /ESCn/PHASE_C / B / A (symbol mirrored so A reads on top; phase order is free, Bluejay sets the direction). J4 and J10 on the top (F), J7 and J13 on the bottom (B), each on its ESC cell's FET side.\n\nMotor wires solder to the land (pads 1/3 1.65 x 1.50, pad 2 0.90 x 1.50) or through the 0.50 mm plated holes: the recommended default. The Molex 53047-0310 PicoBlade header (board side of the hobby 'JST1.25' motor plug, wire side 51021-0300) is a DNP BOM line, out of the CPL, hand-fitted from the far side with its pins trimmed on the land side. Molex rates 1.0 A per contact, -40..85 C, far below the motor current: a plugged motor is a user option that V4 (thermocouple at the header) has to clear before the README recommends it. Mating zone (D72): the plug faces outward over the ear neck, clear of parts.\n\nNet names come from the ESC sheets (the root wires carry no label: /ESCn/PHASE_x). Netclass Phase: directive on M1_A here, the pattern /ESC?/PHASE_? assigns the rest. Phase copper runs from the AGM210MAP phase island straight into the land; solder areas 0.30 mm and phase copper 0.20 mm from the edge (SOLDER_PAD class). M1 rear right (ESC1), M2 front right (ESC2), M3 rear left (ESC3), M4 front left (ESC4): Betaflight quad-X."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 53.34 0)
		(size 167.64 63.5)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ead189ca-2578-5179-a006-3d957446b2af")
	)
	(text_box "PADS: every off-board connection. Style from the OpenFC-Lite-Mini and OpenFC-Lite pads sheets (pads pin down, a rail symbol or a hierarchical label at the wire end, plug blocks in frames); the source of each block is in its note. References, values (pad codes = silk codes), footprints, MPN / Manufacturer / LCSC and the DNP / BOM / CPL attributes are hardware/bom_plan.json; solder pads are DNP and out of BOM and CPL (LINEUP A16), the motor header is a DNP BOM line.\n22 hierarchical labels = the PADS sheet pins (sch_contract.json): VIDEO_IN, M1_A..M4_C, PIOUART0_TX/RX, UART1_TX/RX, LED_STRIP, BUZZER-, USB_D_P/N, VBUS. Rails by power symbol (+BATT_IN, +5V, +5V_CAM, +5V_HD, GND; sources on POWER); VBUS carries its PWR_FLAG here. Netclass directives: VBAT (+BATT_IN at J2), Phase (M1_A), USB (USB_D_P).\nOwed on the bench: J31 pin 1 = GND (prototype 1), J32 pin order (gate G1), motor-header temperature (V4)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.6 241.3 0)
		(size 193.04 43.18)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fc7ab748-ed36-566f-a145-50a38c7fde80")
	)
